{%- comment -%}
  Bare price: no symbol, no currency code, no trailing .00.

  Shopify applies the store's custom money format only to the primary currency.
  Any other Markets currency falls back to Shopify's own formatting, so CAD
  renders "$35.00 CAD" where USD renders "35". Formatting here instead keeps
  every market looking the same.

  Amounts that are not whole keep their cents, which matches how the
  add-to-cart script in theme.liquid formats the button.

  Usage: {% render 'price', amount: product.price %}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign _price = amount | money_without_currency | strip_html | strip -%}
{%- if _price contains '.00' -%}
  {{- _price | remove: '.00' -}}
{%- else -%}
  {{- _price -}}
{%- endif -%}
